# Docker ignore patterns are matched against the path relative to the build
# context, so a bare directory name only matches at the top level. Everything
# below therefore uses the "**/" prefix — without it, the per-package
# node_modules trees, dist folders and turbo caches of the host are copied into
# the image.

# Dependencies (installed inside the image from the lockfile)
**/node_modules

# Build output and caches (rebuilt inside the image)
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/.turbo
**/.tanstack
**/.vinxi
**/.output
**/.wrangler
**/coverage
**/test-results

# Local env files (VITE_SITE_URL is passed as a build arg instead)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc

# Logs and debug output
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# Caches
**/.cache
**/.parcel-cache
**/.eslintcache
**/.tsbuildinfo
**/tmp
**/temp

# OS and editor files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# Docs, CI and agent config (not needed in the image)
README.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
skills-lock.json
.github/
.agents/
**/.git

# Vercel
.vercel
